equal parts give equal keys: true
a changed source changes the key: true
a changed option changes the key: true
parts do not collide by concatenation: true
an added option changes the key: true
enabled at a positive capacity: true
nothing is found before anything is published: true
a published group answers every one of its keys with its value: true
over capacity, the oldest group is evicted whole: true
the younger groups stay: true
a value handed out before its eviction is still the value published: true
the retained bytes are the surviving groups': true
one group was evicted: true
a re-published key answers with the newer group's value: true
evicting the older group (B) left the re-pointed key alone: true
a group larger than the capacity is not retained: true
and evicted nothing to make room for it: true
a lowered capacity evicts the oldest groups down to it: true
capacity 0 disables the cache: true
a lookup at capacity 0 releases everything retained: true
a disabled cache finds nothing: true
and retains nothing published while disabled: true
symbols are renamed by first occurrence: true
kernels differing only in symbol numbers render alike: true
kernels differing in structure stay apart: true
string and character literals are left alone: true
identifiers and numbers merely containing the spelling are left alone: true
comments are renamed like code: true
scope-local names are renamed whole, in the same numbering: true
two lowerings' locals and symbols render alike: true
a local whose node suffix carries a fresh tile id renders alike: true
a v-prefixed name without the scope shape is left alone: true
a quote inside a comment is prose: code after it is still renamed: true
a kept name is left alone whatever its spelling: true
the same kernel under two names and two node numberings renders alike: true
a segment's positional index is dropped, its routine's name kept: true
kernels of two routines stay apart: true
a node's bare and disambiguated spellings render alike: true
two layers' kernels over differently labelled nodes render alike: true
a name outside the bound set is not renamed: true
two parameters stay apart from one parameter used twice: true
swapped operands stay apart: true
a member name is never renamed, even when it spells a bound node: true
so kernels reading different members stay apart: true
attributes and preprocessor lines are copied as they are: true
a bound name that is also a free name disables the node renaming: true
the emitter's derived locals are renamed whole, over a node, a symbol or a uid: true
every template the emitter spells through is listed for the canonical text: true
a derived spelling over an unbound base is left alone: true
different literals stay apart: true
equal keys in one batch compile one representative: true
the duplicate shares the representative's program and symbol: true
a later batch compiles only its misses: true
a hit answers the symbol its code was compiled under, not the current name: true
misses compile as one program per option list, in batch order: true
a refused compile propagates: true
and publishes nothing: true
the next compile of those kernels compiles them afresh: true
two domains missing the same keys compile them once: true
and both get the one program: true
